rented card plan written into docs/rented_gpu.md 2026-09-21 13:40:25, before any rented run: two measurements then a stop (200 steps at the small configuration, and a memory probe), length by points seen not steps, learning rate scaled linearly with batch, one seed each for m0_big_seedA and m1_big_seedA, a difference counts only outside the min to max of the three small seeds, and the upgrade rule is at least 4 of the 6 areas with footprints
run 1 reading written 2026-09-21 14:40, before the run finished and before any of it was read: if m0_rented_small_seedA falls inside the min to max range of the three laptop seeds on in-domain accuracy and on the main San Francisco measures, the machine is not a factor and the large runs may be read as a difference in size; if it falls outside, every comparison of a large run against a small one carries that caveat, written beside the table
run 6 rule written 2026-09-21 14:40, before it runs: each crop is thinned at random to a distinct point count drawn uniformly from 12,800 to 32,768, which is 8.0 to 20.48 points per square metre over a 40 m block. The low end sits below the 11.55 the Swiss training tiles deliver, so the model sees water sparser than it learned it, and the high end is the most a crop can carry, which is what San Francisco and Surrey both deliver. Uniform over the count rather than over the density, drawn per crop, so every batch mixes densities. Reading, also written before: this is a diagnosis on one seed; if water recall comes out above the max of the three existing M1 seeds, that is reported with a proposal for two more seeds and nothing is claimed in the README
